From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:34:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] indexeddb: Write the key generator's current number once per
 transaction

A put that moved the key generator wrote the new current number with an
UPDATE of the object store's row: one more statement per generated key.
The actor keeps the number in the store's row and writes the numbers that
changed once, before the transaction commits and before a schema
operation, which drops the rows; a rollback drops them unwritten.
put_record no longer writes the number; set_key_generator_current_number
does.

Validation: `cargo nextest run -p servo-storage -p servo-storage-traits` (host SQLite): 144 passed, 1 skipped, with test_key_generator_is_written_before_commit_and_schema_changes (reopens the database after the commits; fails when schema operations don't write first) and the key generator and abort tests; `./mach check --ohos -- -p servo-storage --all-targets --no-default-features --features ohos-rdb-backend` and `cargo clippy -p servo-storage --lib -- -D warnings`: no warnings. DAYU200 (QuickJS + RDB, checked-release), 2,000 puts with generated keys into a store without indexes: 1,930/s before, 2,550 and 2,570/s with it (builds with the cursor prefetch of the series in both). The WPT runs of the series are in the last commit of the series (P4.2).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; moved the write to commit and schema operations, added the backend test, measured puts on the board)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
